Session 17 summary — three criteria moved, one root-caused mid-fix:

**Hard rule recorded.** "NEVER reboot clyde" is now RULE 2 in `/src/mxfs/CLAUDE.md`, a permanent ccmemory entry, and the sess15 memory's old "sudo reboot" recovery protocol is overwritten with stop-and-report. No reboot mechanisms remain armed (crontab/atq/systemd clean). Also recorded the timeout/parallelism feedback: every timeout derived per RULE 0 (the 590s reset timeout was 17× the measured 35s — budget now 75s in TIMEOUT_BUDGETS.md), and the reset script's serial verify loop is now parallel.

**zero_silent_loss: PASS** (3/3 iters, 1600/1600 visible each, 355s). The earlier 4800-loss FAIL was contamination from the duplicate-ccloop window plus a harness accounting bug that booked infra mount failures as silent loss — both fixed (mount_cluster retry + `iters_completed` tracking + honest `reason=infra`; criterion timeout 1800→480s). **mkfs_timing: PASS** (531ms).

**crash_consistency: FAILED, root-caused, fix half-built.** 113 fsync-acked records, reader saw 1 — but a fresh mount that claimed the dead writer's log slice recovered all 114 on disk. The data was durably in the dead node's per-node XFS log slice; **v5 never replays a dead peer's slice live** — `v5_lease_expire_cb` only purges locks, and the lazy-drain correctness comment promising "surviving peer replays our journal slot" is unimplemented (the portable journal is vestigial: 0 commits ever). Secondary finding at 16 nodes: a false-fence storm (mutual PR preemption under 10s test leases) livelocked 12 guests — to revisit after the replay fix; the 4-node repro fails identically without it.

**Fix in progress** — live foreign-slice replay on a shadow xlog: foreign-replay opstate bit, intent-family skip in pass2 (keeps the live AIL clean; slice stays dirty so mount-time claimers finish intents; LSN gating makes double-replay safe), and mount-only side-effect gates in `xlog_do_recover`/`xlog_recover` are all written. Remaining: the orchestrator in `xfs_log.c` (private dummy AIL — `xlog_find_tail` writes `ail_head_lsn`), the disklock lowest-live-slot election, the v5 dead-node callback wiring, version bump to 0.5.0, build/deploy/re-run. Full design and edit list are in ccmemory (`sess17-crash-consistency-root-and-foreign-replay-design`).

